 <section class="receipt-invoice-workflow"><h2>Which App Lets You Attach Expense Receipts to a Client Invoice?</h2><p>Zoho Invoice documents both expense receipts and file attachments on invoices. These are separate actions: saving a receipt for your records does not prove the customer can see it.</p><ol><li>Record the expense, upload the receipt and associate it with the relevant customer.</li><li>Mark the expense as billable if the customer agreed to reimburse it.</li><li>Create that customer's invoice and add the billable expense.</li><li>Use the invoice's Upload File option if you need to attach the receipt file to the invoice.</li><li>Preview the recipient-facing email, portal and PDF with a test invoice before using this workflow with a client. Check exactly which files are visible.</li></ol><p>Use the official <a href="https://www.zoho.com/in/invoice/help/expense/expenses.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">expense recording guide</a> and <a href="https://www.zoho.com/en-sg/invoice/help/invoice/new-invoice.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">invoice attachment instructions</a>. Interfaces and features can vary by edition. This is a documentation-based workflow, not a claim that we tested a paid account.</p></section><h2>What freelancers really need from invoicing + expense tracking</h2>
